+## §3 — THE PROOFS IN WRITING (so the kernel checks what is already proved on the page)
+
+**Α1, Theorem T.** Let `C ≤ F₂^P` be the image of `δ¹` and `w̃ ∉ C` a cocycle with `[w̃] = w ≠ 0`. If `0 ∈ w̃ + C` then `w̃ ∈ C`, contradiction; so every `F ∈ w̃ + C` has `|F| ≥ 1`, and `d(w) := min_{F ∈ w̃+C} |F| ≥ 1`. `W_w(y) = Σ_{F ∈ w̃+C} y^{|F|}` has every coefficient below `y^{d(w)}` equal to zero by definition of the minimum, and `W_0(0) = 1` since `0 ∈ C`. Hence `W_w(y)/W_0(y) = m(w) y^{d(w)} + O(y^{d(w)+1})` and, with `y = e^{−2β}`, `Z_w/Z_0 = e^{−2βd(w)}(m(w) + O(e^{−2β}))` — zero to every order in `1/β`. ∎ (ΑΝΗΚΟΥΣΤΟΝ's shape, T-500, one storey down.)
+
+**Α2, the meet.** For `C ≤ F₂^n`, `χ_u(v) = (−1)^{u·v}`, and the orthogonality `Σ_{u∈C^⊥} (−1)^{u·v} = |C^⊥|·[v ∈ C]`: `W_{w+C}(y) = Σ_v y^{|v|} [v−w ∈ C] = |C^⊥|^{−1} Σ_{u∈C^⊥} (−1)^{u·w} Σ_v (−1)^{u·v} y^{|v|} = |C^⊥|^{−1} Σ_{u∈C^⊥} (−1)^{u·w} (1−y)^{|u|}(1+y)^{n−|u|}`, the inner sum factoring over coordinates. On `T³`, `C^⊥ = Z₂(Λ) = B¹(Λ*) ⊕ ⟨h̃⟩`, and for `u = ∂ + h̃` with `∂` a coboundary of the dual, `u·w̃ = h̃·w̃` since a coboundary pairs to zero with a cocycle; so the sum over `C^⊥` is the sum over the twists `h` of `(−1)^{⟨h,w⟩}` times the wall enumerator of the twisted Ising model, `J_h[k]/2` wall sets of weight `k`. ∎ That is the identity Α0's T3 decides on the record's data, with `|C^⊥| = 2^{V+2}`.
+
+**Α3, even time.** Reflect `T³` through the plane between time slices `t` and `t+1` (even extent: the plane and its antipode are both between slices). Gauge-fix the links crossing the plane to the identity; then the Wilson weight factors as `e^{βS_+}·e^{βS_−}` with `S_−` the reflection of `S_+`, and for `f` a function of the upper half, `⟨Θf, f⟩ = Σ_{boundary} |Σ_{upper} e^{βS_+} f|² ≥ 0`. At odd extent the two reflection planes cannot both lie between slices, and ΑΝΤΑΥΓΕΙΑ's counted negative eigenvalues are the refusal. ∎ (Osterwalder–Seiler's argument; ΑΝΤΑΥΓΕΙΑ's placement of the evenness.)
