+difference of gluon loops. Split the loop momentum at k₀ and subtract each half's zero-momentum value. The ultraviolet half is
+bounded. The infrared half carries the continuum logarithm 8b₀ ln(1/p). The remainders gain two powers of momentum and contribute
+bounded constants.
