+**16.49 STAKE — THE GROWTH BOUND FOR CLOSED SURFACES: SHAPE (ii) REFUTED AT THE DESK, THE UNTYPED POTENTIAL'S FLOOR, AND THE RIGOROUS TAIL FROM THE CLOSING TREE'S ALIVE-NODE CENSUS (09:5x EDT; written before `g47_closing.c` runs; the plan seat's order of 09:4x: a rigorous growth bound μ < 5 for connected branch-free closed surfaces of `ℤ⁴` through a plaquette, which sets the reach of its surface KP — μ ≤ 4 gives 0.678 and μ ≤ 3 gives 0.88, against 0.5465 with `N(F) ≤ 5^{F−1}`).** (a) **THE COMPLETION-COUNT SHAPE (ii) IS REFUTED.** Let `D(m)` be the maximum over nodes of the completions with exactly `m` more plaquettes. Then `D(1) = 1`: a node completes in one plaquette only when its open links bound a unit square, and the filler is unique. So `D(m)^{1/m}` cannot bound μ. A completion of the root passes through OPEN nodes, so completion counts do not compose. (b) **THE POTENTIAL SHAPE (i) WITHOUT TYPES HAS A FLOOR.** Take `φ = x^k`, with `k` the open-link count; adding a plaquette with `j` already-open other links changes `k` by `2 − 2j`. A supersolution then needs `Σ_{valid q} x^{2−2j(q)} ≤ μ` at the chosen link of every node. At a unit hole the filler gives `x^{−4}` and the four out-of-plane expansions give `x²` each, and `min_x (x^{−4} + 4x²) = 2^{2/3} + 4·2^{−1/3} = 4.762`, at `x⁶ = ½`. At the lexicographically extreme link the three candidates on the far side can each fill a notch (`3x^{−4} + 2`, against the sparse `5x²`), so the untyped bound returns to 5 if that configuration is reachable. A gain needs link TYPES; that is staked UNGUESSED with the 4.762 floor and no promise of μ ≤ 4. (c) **THE RIGOROUS LEVER TAKEN NOW: THE TAIL.** Every closed surface of area `F > F₀` passes through an alive node `P` at depth `n₀ < F − 1` of the closing tree (smallest open link, branch-free; each surface is a complete leaf exactly once). From `P` each step has at most five valid candidates and lowers the open-link count by at most four, so `Σ_{F>F₀} N(F)u^F ≤ Σ_{P alive, depth n₀} u^{n₀+1}(5u)^{max(F₀ − n₀, ⌈k(P)/4⌉)}/(1 − 5u)` for `5u < 1`. Its `n₀ = 0` case is the plan seat's present tail. THE INSTRUMENT `g47_closing.c` counts the alive nodes by depth and open-link count, `H_n(k)`, with no storage. KNOWN ANSWERS: its complete leaves at depths 5, 9, 11, 13 read 4, 60, 80, 1092 in `ℤ⁴`, and 2, 10, 70, 16, 498 at depths 5, 9, 13, 15, 17 in `ℤ³`. STAKES: the alive-node ratio `A(n)/A(n−1)` settles between 4.0 and 4.6 by `n = 12` (UNGUESSED within that range). At `u = 0.136` (the plan seat's reach, `F₀ = 22`), the tail bound from the deepest `n₀` reached falls below the `n₀ = 0` form by a factor between 0.02 and 0.3 — about one order, which moves the reach toward 0.6, not to 0.88. (d) The lattice designs `S = Λ + B` (`g46_lattice.c`, written before the row closed): the `ℤ³` control finds the single site admissible exactly on the bcc lattice (index 4) and the bcc pair on `2ℤ³` among others; its `ℤ⁴` run over every sublattice of index ≤ 40 and nine cluster shapes is recorded in its file when it ends, and the row is closed either way.
