+**16.58 STAKE — LEMMA P (THE ODD RULE) AND LEMMA W′ (WALLS ON ANY REST), PROVED ON THE PAGE, AND THE NEXT INSTRUMENT'S READINGS STAKED BEFORE `g48_polymers_v7.c` EXISTS (11:5x EDT).** Notation: `m_X(l)` is the number of plaquettes of `X` at the link `l`; `X` is CLOSED if every `m_X(l)` is 0 or at least 2, EVEN if every `m_X(l)` is even; a CONTACT link has multiplicity at least 4; `X` is `Z₂`-MINIMAL if it is even and no nonempty proper subset of it is even. (i) **LEMMA P.** Fix a total order on links and a plaquette `p0`. The ODD-RULE TREE `T_odd` has root `{p0}`; a node `S` with a link of odd multiplicity has the children `S + q` for every plaquette `q ∉ S` containing its smallest odd link; a node with no odd link is a leaf. A node has exactly `6 − m_S(l)` children at its smallest odd link `l` — 5 at multiplicity 1, 3 at multiplicity 3 — so `T_odd` has at most `5^{F−1}` leaves of area `F`, counted with multiplicity. (P1) Every `Z₂`-minimal `X ∋ p0` is a leaf, reached by EVERY path that stays inside `X`: along such a path `S ⊊ X` is not even (it is nonempty and `X` is minimal), so it has a smallest odd link `l`; `m_X(l)` is even and `m_S(l)` odd, so `X ∖ S` holds an odd number, at least 1, of plaquettes at `l`, and a child inside `X` exists; the path stops at the first even subset of `X` containing `p0`, which is `X`. (P2) An even IRREDUCIBLE `X` (no split into two closed parts sharing a forest) whose contact links form a forest is `Z₂`-minimal: if a nonempty proper `S ⊊ X` were even, `S` and `X ∖ S` would both be even, hence closed, and a link they share has multiplicity at least 2 in each, so at least 4 in `X` — a contact link; the shared links would lie in the forest of contacts, form a forest, and make `X` reducible. (P3) Every closed even set is a disjoint union of `Z₂`-minimal pieces (remove a minimal nonempty even subset and repeat); each piece is link-connected, and for a link-connected set the graph of pieces sharing a link is connected. So the 576 pinches at `F = 18`, the 3,840 pinches and 960 double contacts at `F = 20`, and every even irreducible set with acyclic contacts are leaves of the tree that counts the surfaces: the bound `5^{F−1}` covers the surfaces and these sets TOGETHER, at no extra count. What (P2) leaves of the even irreducibles is the contact CYCLES — the waists, 64 at `F = 16` and 2,340 at `F = 20` — which (P3) counts as pieces on a contact graph, as the composites are counted, with a cycle in place of the forest. (ii) **LEMMA W′ — WALLS ON ANY REST.** Let `R` be closed and even, branched or not, connected or not, with EXCESS `E(R) = Σ_l (m_R(l)/2 − 1)`, which is at least 0 and zero iff `R` is branch-free. From `Σ_l m_R(l) = 4|R|`: (W1) `#links(R) = 2|R| − E(R)`; (W2) the plaquettes outside `R` touching it, each counted once per touching link, number `Σ_{l ∈ R} (6 − m_R(l)) = 8|R| − 6E(R)`; (W3) the single walls (`q ∉ R` with all four links in `R`) number at most `(8|R| − 6E)/4 = 2|R| − (3/2)E(R)`. (W4) Split the integer-spin plaquettes `Y` into PATCHES, the components under adjacency through links NOT in `R`. Admissibility factors over patches: at a link of `R`, `m_R(l)` is even and at least 2, and `½^{⊗m_R} ⊗ 1^{⊗k}` contains the trivial representation for every `k ≥ 0` (`½ ⊗ ½ ⊇ 0 ⊕ 1`); off `R`, `1^{⊗k}` contains it iff `k ≠ 1`. So a patch is exactly a set closed off `R`, and patches interact only by hard core and through the link-integral factors at shared links of `R`. (W5) When `R ∪ Y` is link-connected, every patch touches `R`: a patch with no link in `R` shares no link with `R` or with another patch. A patch with at least 2 plaquettes whose off-`R` links all have multiplicity 2 is generated from any of its plaquettes touching `R` by the forced closing path on off-`R` links, so those with `n` plaquettes through a given root number at most `5^{n−1}`. Hence the wall gas on `R`, with positive weights and the hard core dropped, is at most `exp( η·(2|R| − 1.5E) + (8|R| − 6E)·η·5η/(1 − 5η) + B )`, where `η` is the spin-1 activity and `B` the patches with a branched off-`R` link — the spin-1 sector's own branched polymers, bounded by any bound valid for all closed sets at activity `η`. Every term is its branch-free value MINUS a nonnegative multiple of `E(R)`: a branched rest has fewer wall sites than a surface of its area, and a disconnected rest is two polymers joined by a bridge patch, which the KP tree counts. So the plan seat's step (3) holds for every rest with the constants of the branch-free case. The link-integral factors at wall-on-rest links are per link and bounded: `dim Inv(½^{⊗m} ⊗ 1^{⊗k})` is 1, 2, 3 at `(m, k)` = (2, 1), (2, 2), (4, 1), against 1, 1, 2 without the wall. (iii) **STAKED — THE ODD-RULE REACHABILITY CENSUS** (`g48_polymers_v7.c`, written after this paragraph: for every even set `X ∋ p0` of the census, `T_odd` run inside `X` from the root `p0` and from every root `r ∈ X`, under the lattice order of link ids, by a search over subsets of `X` with a memo). KNOWN ANSWERS from (P1)–(P2): every branch-free set, every pinch and every double contact is reached from EVERY root, 100% at every area; a single miss convicts the instrument or the lemma. UNGUESSED: the waists and the even reducible sets, from `p0` and from all roots. A non-minimal set can fail because its path may stop at a proper even subset: two cubes touching at one link, rooted on one cube, fail under any order that closes that cube before the contact link becomes its smallest odd link. (iv) **STAKED — THE BRANCHED RESTS BY PROFILE:** at `F = 19` every rest of (26/4/3) is REDUCIBLE and every rest of (30/4/1) is IRREDUCIBLE (a pinch). How the three contact links of a (26/4/3) rest connect is UNGUESSED (three links bound no cycle, so they always form a forest). The split of the 1,205 reducible rests at `|Y| = 3` between (24/8/1) and (25/6/2) is UNGUESSED. (v) **STAKED — THE TWO-BOX WAIST BUILT:** for each of the 20 plaquettes `P ≠ p0` sharing a cube with `p0`, the mod-2 sum of the boundaries of the four cubes on `P` has area 20, contains `p0`, is even with profile (32/0/4), is IRREDUCIBLE (its four cups are its components through multiplicity-2 links, and a closed split takes two cups on each side, which share the 4-cycle `∂P`), and decomposes with least cycle rank 1 and exactly three separating pairings. Its reachability belongs to (iii)'s unguessed column.
