+**16.60 STAKE — THE WEIGHTS: THE EXACT HAAR INTEGRAL OF EVERY IRREDUCIBLE POLYMER TO AREA 18, BY PROFILE (12:1x EDT; the plan seat's order of 12:0x and 12:1x — S1 §10–§11 of III-Yang_Mills, commits 2dd4824 and 7a51150: the counting half of R1 here, the weights half there, and this table its falsifier; written before `g50_weights.c` exists).** THE INSTRUMENT. For each irreducible `X` of the census and each spin assignment with ½ on an even `R ⊆ X` and 1 on `X ∖ R`, it computes `I = ∫ Π_l dU_l Π_p χ_{j_p}(U_p)` as a tensor network. There is one tensor per link, `T_l = ∫ dU ⊗_{p ∋ l} D^{j_p}(U^{±1})`, whose entries are exact from `∫ a^p ā^q b^r b̄^s dU = δ_{pq} δ_{rs} p! r!/(p+r+1)!` on `U = [[a, b], [−b̄, ā]]`; spin 1 acts on quadratic forms in `(x, y)` with integer polynomial entries. There is one bond per plaquette corner, and the network is contracted greedily modulo `2^61 − 1` and `2^62 − 57` and in floating point; the rational is read back by Wang's reconstruction from the residues and checked against the float. REPORTED: `ρ(X) = W(X)/(u^{F−|Y|}(3a₁)^{|Y|}) = Σ_{least Y} 2^{F−|Y|} I(X; X ∖ Y)`, with `u = a_½/a₀`, `a₁ = a₁/a₀`, `d_½ a_½/a₀ = 2u` and `d₁a₁/a₀ = 3a₁`, tallied by profile together with the rest's `χ`. Also reported: the full sum at spins ≤ 1, `Σ_{R even, admissible} (2u)^{|R|}(3a₁)^{|X ∖ R|} I(X; R)`, as its coefficients; a set is admissible iff no link has `m_R = 0` and `m_{X∖R} = 1`. KNOWN ANSWERS: every orientable branch-free surface to `F = 16` reads `ρ = 2^χ` (`I = 2^{χ−F}`: 4 on spheres, 1 on tori), with `χ` counted from vertex cycles; and the 66 chambers of `F = 11` read `ρ = 4`. By hand: each cup gives `2^{4−8} χ_½(U_γ)` (the cube check, cup plus a spin-½ lid, gives `2^{−4} = 2^{χ−F}`), and `∫ χ_½ χ_½ χ₁ = 1`, so `I = 2^{−8}` and `ρ = 2^{10}·2^{−8} = 4`. THE PLAN SEAT'S STAKES, recorded as theirs (S1 §11): W1 — every single-wall chamber with a branch-free rest `S` reads `±2^{χ(S)}`, so +4 for a sphere rest; W2 — every pinch reads `W/u^F = 2^{