+**16.58-b THE PROOFS OF LEMMA P AND OF THE SITE AND ROOT COUNTS, WRITTEN OUT FOR THE TRUNK (13:2x EDT; the trunk seat's lane items B2–B3 of 13:2x; nothing above edited; each statement is the one 16.58 made, the proof given in full).** Conventions: a plaquette set `X`; `m_X(l)` the number of its plaquettes at the link `l`; CLOSED iff every `m_X(l) ∈ {0} ∪ [2, ∞)`; EVEN iff every `m_X(l)` is even; `Z₂`-MINIMAL iff even and no nonempty proper subset is even; a CONTACT link has `m_X(l) ≥ 4`; REDUCIBLE iff `X = X₁ ⊔ X₂` with both parts closed and the links they share forming a forest. **LEMMA P.** *Fix a total order on links and a plaquette `p₀`. Let `T` be the tree with root `{p₀}` in which a node `S` with an odd link has, at its smallest odd link `l`, the children `S ∪ {q}` for every plaquette `q ∉ S` containing `l`, and a node with no odd link is a leaf. (P1) Every `Z₂`-minimal `X ∋ p₀` is a leaf of `T`, and every path of `T` that stays inside `X` ends at `X`. (P2) Every even irreducible `X` whose contact links form a forest is `Z₂`-minimal. (P3) A node has `6 − m_S(l)` children, hence at most 5, so `T` has at most `5^{F−1}` leaves of area `F` counted with multiplicity, and the leaves of area `F` contain every `Z₂`-minimal even set and every even irreducible set with acyclic contacts through `p₀`.* Proof of (P1). Let `S ⊊ X` be a node on a path inside `X` (the root `{p₀} ⊆ X` is one). `S` is nonempty and proper, so it is not even by minimality; let `l` be its smallest odd link. `m_X(l)` is even and `m_S(l)` is odd, so `m_X(l) − m_S(l)` is odd and positive: some `q ∈ X ∖ S` contains `l`, and `S ∪ {q}` is a child inside `X`. The path therefore continues until it reaches an even node, and the even nodes inside `X` containing `p₀` are the even subsets of `X` containing `p₀`, of which by minimality `X` is the only nonempty one. ∎ Proof of (P2). Suppose `S` is a nonempty proper even subset of `X`. Then `X ∖ S` is even (a difference of even multiplicities), both are closed (even and nonzero means at least 2), and at every link they share `m_X = m_S + m_{X∖S} ≥ 4`, so the shared links are contact links; a subset of a forest is a forest; so `(S, X ∖ S)` is a reducing split, contradicting irreducibility. ∎ Proof of (P3). At the smallest odd link `l` of `S`, exactly `m_S(l)` of the 6 plaquettes of `ℤ⁴` containing `l` are in `S` and the rest are children; `m_S(l) ≥ 1` gives at most 5. A leaf of area `F` sits at depth `F − 1`. ∎ **THE COUNTS ON A CLOSED EVEN REST `R` WITH EXCESS `E(R) = Σ_l (m_R(l)/2 − 1)` over its links.** (W1) `#links(R) = 2|R| − E(R)`: `Σ_l m_R(l) = 4|R|` and `Σ_l (m_R(l)/2 − 1) = 2|R| − #links`. (W2) `Σ_{l ∈ R} (6 − m_R(l)) = 6·#links − 4|R| = 8|R| − 6E(R)`, which counts the pairs (plaquette `q ∉ R`, link `l ∈ R ∩ q`). (W3) A single wall is a `q ∉ R` with all four links in `R`, so it is counted four times in (W2): at most `(8|R| − 6E)/4 = 2|R| − 1.5E(R)` single walls. (W5) *Let `Y` be a patch: a set of plaquettes outside `R`, link-connected through links NOT in `R`, with `m_Y(l) = 2` at every such off-`R` link, and let `p ∈ Y` be given. Then at most `5^{n−1}` such patches of `n` plaquettes contain `p`.* Proof. Build `P₀ = {p}`, and while the partial set `P_k ⊆ Y` has an off-`R` link of multiplicity 1 in `P_k`, let `l` be the smallest and set `P_{k+1} = P_k ∪ {q}` for the plaquette `q ∈ Y ∖ P_k` containing `l` (it exists and is unique: `m_Y(l) = 2` and `m_{P_k}(l) = 1`). The construction stays inside `Y` and terminates; at termination every off-`R` link of `P_k` has multiplicity 0 or 2 in `P_k`. If `P_k ≠ Y`, link-connectedness through off-`R` links gives `q′ ∈ Y ∖ P_k` and an off-`R` link `l′` shared by `q′` and some plaquette of `P_k`; then `m_{P_k}(l′) = 1` (exactly one of the two plaquettes of `Y` at `l′` lies in `P_k`), contradicting termination. So `P_k = Y` after exactly `n − 1` steps, and `Y` is determined by the choices made, each among the at most 5 plaquettes containing `l` other than the one in `P_k`. ∎ (Admissibility, for the record: at a link of `R`, `m_R(l)` is even and at least 2 and `½^{⊗m} ⊗ 1^{⊗k}` contains the trivial representation for every `k ≥ 0`, so patches are constrained only off `R`, where `1^{⊗k}` contains it iff `k ≠ 1`.) What (W5) does NOT cover, said plainly for B4: a patch with an off-`R` link of multiplicity 3 or more, and a patch that is a union of closed sub-patches — the construction above stops at the first closed sub-patch. Those are B4's objects.
