+**16.65 THE DRESSING LEMMA — B4 PAID: EVERY ADMISSIBLE SPIN-1 PATCH, BRANCHED OR COMPOSITE, COUNTED WITH ITS ACTIVITY BY A FIXED POINT, PROVED (13:3x EDT; the trunk seat's lane item B4 of 13:2x; desk work, no instrument; nothing above edited).** SETTING. `U` is a closed set of plaquettes (the rest, or a rest already dressed); OFF-`U` links are the links not in `U`. A PIECE on `U` is a nonempty set `Q` of plaquettes disjoint from `U`, link-connected through off-`U` links, with `m_Q(l) ≠ 1` at every off-`U` link `l` not in... — precisely: ADMISSIBLE RELATIVE TO `U` means every off-`U` link `l` with `m_Q(l) = 1` lies in `U`'s link set; MINIMAL means no proper nonempty sub-piece through its root is admissible relative to `U`. A DECORATION of `U` is a finite set `Δ` of plaquettes disjoint from `U` such that `U ∪ Δ` is admissible (every link of `U ∪ Δ` outside `U` has multiplicity `≠ 1` in `Δ`, links of `U` unconstrained); `|Δ|` its size. `z > 0` is the activity per plaquette (for the fold-in `z = 3a₁·e`, the KP factor included). **THE TWO SITE CLASSES.** (i) A piece of size 1 is a plaquette all of whose four links lie in `U` ∪ (the rest of the decoration); rooted on `U` alone it is a SINGLE WALL of `U`, and (W3) counts those: at most `2|U| − 1.5E(U) ≤ 2|U|`. (ii) A piece of size `s ≥ 2` has a root plaquette sharing an off-`U`... — a root sharing a link with `U`: at most `5` per link of `U` and `≤ 4|U|` links, so `≤ 20|U|` roots, and by the closing argument of 16.58-b (W5) with "close the smallest off-`U` link of multiplicity 1 by any of the `≤ 5` plaquettes containing it; a link of `U` is never closed" at most `5^{s−1}` minimal pieces of size `s` through a root — the proof is (W5)'s verbatim with "multiplicity 2" replaced by "multiplicity at least 2" (a link with `m_Q(l) ≥ 2` and `m_P(l) = 1` has a plaquette of `Q ∖ P`), which is why the lemma covers multiplicities `≥ 3`. **THE DECOMPOSITION.** Every decoration `Δ` of `U` is a disjoint union of minimal pieces: let `Q₁` be the minimal admissible-relative-to-`U` piece through the smallest plaquette of `Δ` (the closing construction from it inside `Δ` ends at one); then `Δ ∖ Q₁` is a decoration of `U ∪ Q₁`; iterate. Each piece is determined by its root plaquette and its closing choices; a decoration is determined by the SET of its pieces (order forgotten). Pieces rooted on `U` (sharing a link with `U`, or all links in `U` for size 1) are FIRST-LEVEL; every other piece is rooted on an earlier piece, so a decoration of `U` is a set of first-level pieces each carrying a decoration of itself — a decoration of `Q` as base, where "rooted on `Q`" means sharing a link of `Q` not in `U`. **LEMMA (the dressing).** *Let `g(κ) = 2 z e^{κ} + 20·Σ_{s ≥ 2} 5^{s−1} z^{s} e^{κ s} = 2 z e^{κ} + 100 z² e^{2κ} / (1 − 5 z e^{κ})` on `5 z e^{κ} < 1`. If `κ* > 0` satisfies `g(κ*) ≤ κ*`, then for every closed `U`, `D(U) := Σ_{Δ decoration of U} z^{|Δ|} ≤ exp(κ* |U|)`.* Proof, by induction on the size of `U ∪ Δ` over the finite sets that can occur at fixed total size `N` (the statement is proved for all decorations of size `≤ N − |U|`, `N` arbitrary). Write a decoration as a set `{Q_i}` of first-level pieces, each with a decoration `Δ_i` of `Q_i` as base (relative to `U ∪ Q_i`); the map is injective. Then `D(U) ≤ Σ_{sets of first-level pieces} Π_i [z^{|Q_i|} D_rel(Q_i)]`, and by induction `D_rel(Q_i) ≤ e^{κ* |Q_i|}` (its decorations are smaller). A set of items each carrying a weight `w(item) ≥ 0` has `Σ_{subsets} Π w ≤ exp(Σ_{items} w)` (expand the product `Π (1 + w)`). The items are the first-level pieces of `U`: `≤ 2|U|` of size 1, weight `z e^{κ*}`, and `≤ 20|U|·5^{s−1}` of size `s ≥ 2`, weight `z^{s} e^{κ* s}`. So `D(U) ≤ exp(|U| g(κ*)) ≤ exp(κ* |U|)`. ∎ (The induction's base is the empty decoration, weight 1.) **THE NUMBERS.** `g` is increasing and convex in `κ` on its domain, so the least fixed point `κ*(z)` exists iff `min_κ (g(κ) − κ) ≤ 0`, and the fold-in reads it by bisection at its `z`: at `z = 0.