+**The status alphabet, infix-free (law 46):** PROVED (with its discharge site) · LEAN (the file, built, its theorem count) · REDUCED (to a named lemma) · MEASURED (an exact reading with no supremum and no proof) · READ (a literature reading, the page named) · REFUTED (with its killer) · STAKED (written before its run; unrun, or run and held) · NAMED (a missing object with its falsifier) · CLAIM-ONLY (green only when consumed outside this tree). The sources: the pages of this repository (OPEN/, OPEN/ledger/, records/, kernel/, source/ground/), the III tree (DOCS/III-APERANTON-THE-BOUNDLESS-PREREGISTRATION.md and its Addenda I–II, DOCS/III-PENTAPYLON-THE-FIVE-GATES-PREREGISTRATION.md, DOCS/III-KATATAXIS-THE-RANKING-OF-THE-FIELDS.md, DOCS/III-TOMEUS-THE-CUTTER-PREREGISTRATION.md, DOCS/III-STROPHINX-THE-HINGE-PREREGISTRATION.md, DOCS/III-ANEXALEIPTON-THE-INEFFACEABLE-PREREGISTRATION.md, LEAN/aperanton/, STDLIB/build/aperanton/, STDLIB/build/pentapylon/), the memory corpus (77 notes naming the line, the 855 KB ledger of the Yang–Mills seat among them, its 268 paragraph heads read), the five scratchpads of this machine's seats (the only lines bearing on the line were the C-1 correction note and this seat's own drafts), and the three live seats' answers by message (iii-73: nothing beyond HEAD; iii-24: the window-module theorem, the rank sentence, the §26 proposal, named below under its seat; iii-58: the certified-enclosure doors, named in §5).
