+## 7. The synthesis — the trunk seat's, a desk argument written as a STAKE with its kill-switch
+
+**The constraints that were belief, two.** (i) *"A finite computation implies decay only through a supremum over boundary data."* The tower's law of total covariance (Tower.lean, TowerChain.lean, MassGapAssembly.lean) composes scales with the coarse MEASURE'S OWN average: cov(f, g) = ⟨cov(f, g | coarse data)⟩_coarse + cov_coarse(E f, E g), and no configuration is coupled across data. The supremum is a tool's choice, inherited from Dobrushin's comparison theorem, not physics; what the frustrated datum (0.649) killed is the supremum, and what the Gaussian field killed is the coupling of configurations across data (the annealed per-site product). (ii) *"The chessboard constant is useless at β = 2.2."* It was read with the i.i.d. trial measure in tree gauge; the Gibbs variational principle admits any trial measure, and the one-step blocked marginal — exact on the cube and tube engines — is the right one.
+
+**The missing object in its honest form** (§95's "multi-scale treatment of large fields by probability", with the tower as its composition): at each scale, the fibre term ⟨cov(f, g | d)⟩ bounded by Dobrushin's criterion on GAUGE-INVARIANT coarse variables read at TYPICAL coarse data (the 10⁻³ response, falling with β), plus the atypical (frustrated) data's share bounded by (their chessboard weight) × (a trivial covariance bound); the coarse term bounded by the same criterion at the next scale. At the desk it survives both falsifiers by construction: in U(1)'s Coulomb phase the typical-data part FAILS (the weighted row sums diverge), as it must; the free field has no frustrated data and algebraic influence, so it fails the typical-data part too. What the desk does NOT settle is whether the typical set has a usable measure at the crossover.
+
+**THE NEXT EXPERIMENT (Κ3's datum made exact; STAKED here before any instrument):** the frustrated-plaquette weight P(tr U_p ≤ 0) at β = 2.2 under a block-cluster trial measure built from the one-step blocked marginal on the exact 2×2×2 cube and 2×2×L tube engines at spins ≤ 2, by thermodynamic integration (RESULTS 17 (U4)), beside the i.i.d. reading already in hand (near 0.1); two-sided: U(1) at β = 1.2 must NOT be parted from SU(2) by the weight alone (its typical-data part is what fails), the free field's weight is 0; KILL-SWITCH: a weight at or above 0.05 per plaquette under every computable trial measure means the dilute accounting cannot start at the crossover and the bridge [β*, ≈ 2.5] needs another description — then the strong end must be pushed past 1 (the gas's own measured ceiling) before any bridge is attempted. Falsifier of the stake's premise: the 0.1 already read was the i.i.d. trial's; if the block-cluster trial does not lower it, (ii) above was not belief.
