+**§9 ADDENDUM RESULTS — THE OSCILLATION READ AT THE THREE STRONGEST LINKS, AND THE CHAIN OF INEQUALITIES THAT PLACES THE LADDER (2026-11-01 12:1x EST, read from `date`; the trunk seat; two passes of the instrument W2_SET, every value from its records).** THE CHAIN, in THE GROUND's own symbols (Hypothesis I verbatim: "there are numbers κ > 0 and α < 1 and a rung j₀ such that at every rung j ≥ j₀, on every lattice of the construction, Σ_{y′} C^λ_j(y, y′) e^{κ|y−y′|} ≤ α for every coarse point y", C^λ_j(y, y′) the interdependence coefficient of the blocked measure, and §8's reading C^λ_j(y, y′) ≤ 1 − e^{−Δ_{yy′}(A)} with Δ the mixed second difference of the effective action): at a fixed fine configuration of every link but ℓ, (i) the ladder's moment influence |ΔE[χ_a(A)]|/d_a at the angle π is at most the total-variation distance of the loop's two laws at that angle; (ii) that distance is at most the link's OSCILLATION, the sup over the link's two values; (iii) the oscillation at one configuration is at most β_{Aℓ}, its sup over configurations; (iv) by the ADDENDUM's inequality Σ_{ℓ∈B} sup β_{Aℓ} ≥ b_{AB} = C^λ(A, B). The ladder reads (i); this instrument reads a lower bound on (ii) — the range of E[χ_½(A)] over a grid of the link's values at the ordered datum. THE READINGS (pass 1: 391 unit quaternions, fifteen half-angles by twenty-six axes; the π rotation about x is the ladder's point): link 56 (the one-step object's strongest, the x-link (−1, 2, 0, 0)): base E₁ 0.621039, the π point moves it by 0.0329, the grid's largest deviation 0.0590 and its oscillation (max − min) 0.0703; link 60 (the y-link (0, 1, 0, −1)): 0.0282, 0.0535, 0.0645; link 78 (the two-step object's strongest, the y-link (0, 2, 0, −1)): base 0.145567, 0.0091, 0.0173, 0.0209. So THE LADDER'S ONE-ANGLE READING IS 44–47 % OF THE ONE-LINK OSCILLATION AT EVERY LINK READ, at both scales; the grid's extremal values sit at the same two quaternions for all three links (a rotation of 337.5° about an axis in the xz-plane at the maximum, of 247.5° about another at the minimum), and the two scales' strongest links oscillate in the ratio 0.0209/0.0703 = 0.30, as their π readings do (0.28). THE SECOND PASS FOUND THE STRUCTURE (osc2_links.sh: the half-turn about 203 axes, the coordinate axes exact, and the angle scan about x): AT THE ORDERED DATUM THE MOMENT DEPENDS ON THE VARIED LINK THROUGH ITS CLASS ALONE — at the half-turn, all 203 axes read one value to twelve digits at every link (0.588140843 at link 56, 0.592802956 at 60, 0.136422132 at 78) — because every other outside link is the identity, the plaquette weights and the loop's character are class functions and the Haar measure is conjugation-invariant, so a global conjugation carries the object with link ℓ = U into the object with ℓ = gUg⁻¹: the single-link oscillation at this datum is a function of one variable, w = cos(angle/2) on [−1, 1], and the π rotation is its value at w = 0. THE EXACT OSCILLATION (wscan_links.sh: 181 rotation angles 0..360° about x, the extremes bracketed to two degrees; records wscan_*): link 56 — base 0.621039, maximum 0.635430 at 360° (the CENTRE FLIP, U = −1, which raises the loop's expectation above the aligned datum's), minimum 0.560878 at 240°, oscillation 0.07455, the π point 0.441 of it; link 60 — 0.635055 at 360°, 0.566766 at 240°, oscillation 0.06829, the π point 0.413 of it; link 78 (two steps) — base 0.145567, 0.150147 at 360°, 0.128034 at 240°, oscillation 0.02211, the π point 0.414 of it. So the ladder's one-angle reading is 41–44 % of the exact one-link oscillation at the three strongest links, the extremes lie on the centre-flipped side of SU(2) at both scales, and the two scales' oscillations stand in the ratio 0.0221/0.0746 = 0.30 as their π readings do (0.28). WHAT THIS PLACES: a row sum read at the oscillation instead of the π point would be about twice the ladder's at the strongest links (0.712 → of order 1.5 at one step, 0.395 → of order 0.9 at two, if the ratio held across the row, which is not read); it is still (iii)'s lower bound at ONE configuration, with the sup over SU(2)^{532} untaken, and §9 ADDENDUM's conclusion stands unmoved: the direction by scale (×0.55, ×0.36 at the two data) is what the objects read, and the theorem is the sup. THE RECORDS: osc_n2_W2L1_link56.txt, osc_n2_W2L1_link60.txt, osc_n4_W2L1_link78.txt, osc2_*.txt, the two frozen scripts, under records/surface-gas/oscillation.
