y shapes (a b with b⁻¹a⁻¹b; a b with b⁻¹a) have equal Z₂-classes and are not minimal. So every minimal sphere-sheet set with at most three faces over at most two independent contact cycles has primitive face words and reads S = 4 — the theta reading ½ → 4 of (6) is the general case here, not an instance. (4) WHAT REMAINS. For m ≥ 4 or r ≥ 3 the budget still bounds the words (total non-trivial length ≤ 4r over m − 1 words of independent Z₂-classes) but no argument yet makes the system primitive; a non-primitive system with independent mod-2 classes needs a word like a²b²a⁻¹b⁻¹ (primitive abelianisation, not primitive), which the budget forbids on two chords and permits in principle on more. The conjecture stands on exactly this: SHORT WORDS WITH INDEPENDENT CLASSES ARE PRIMITIVE SYSTEMS — a statement about free groups with a combinatorial budget, decidable case by case by Whitehead's algorithm on any object the enumerator produces, which is what the two-road reader will do when the Weingarten step is built (today it refuses r ≥ 2: 124 leaves to F = 26, every one read S ≤ 4 by the resolution road). The next instrument is that step; the next object a minimal sphere-sheet set with four faces, which no census has produced.
 
